   "dir": "/Volumes/T7/guided-analysis/tools/bench-runs/2026-10-09/claude_claude-haiku-5-5/nair2024-plasmid-growth/run1/home/sessions/20261008-232644-b347",
   "answer": "## Result: this test does not show that any plasmid lowers the growth rate\n\nThe data do not show a reduction in growth rate for any plasmid. No plasmid has a p value below 0.05. This does not prove that the plasmids have no effect. Several confidence intervals are wide and include values well below 1.\n\nI also removed a wavelength number that I had written without a tool result behind it.\n\n## What I did\n\n1. Fit a logistic growth curve to each well with growthcurver 4.6.1. The input was the time column and the optical density (OD) wells, in hours.\n2. Used these settings, from your decisions:\n   - Background correction: min.\n   - Blank wells: none.\n   - Last time point: 0, which means all points.\n   - Time unit: h.\n   - Excluded wells: W10 to W18 and W80 to W84. These are all wells of blocks 2 and 12.\n   - Lag time: not calculated, because you did not ask for it.\n3. Divided the r of each well by the r of the Host well of the same block. The reference rule was same block.\n4. Tested each plasmid mean against 1 with a two-sided one-sample t test.\n5. Calculated the mean of the 12 plasmid relative means.\n\nThe fit gave 70 wells with no growthcurver note. I looked at the plot. In most wells, the red fitted curve follows the grey readings closely.\n\n## Results\n\nHost r was 0.3805 per h (n = 10, one Host well per block; SD 0.0092 per h).\n\nEach plasmid has n = 5 blocks. The relative rate is the r of the plasmid well divided by the r of the Host well of the same block.\n\n| Plasmid | Mean relative rate | 95% CI | p value (against 1) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| P1 | 1.0053 | 0.9079 to 1.1027 | 0.887 |\n| P2 | 1.0278 | 0.9192 to 1.1364 | 0.517 |\n| P3 | 1.0329 | 0.9183 to 1.1476 | 0.470 |\n| P4 | 0.9657 | 0.7957 to 1.1357 | 0.605 |\n| P5 | 1.0725 | 0.9254 to 1.2195 | 0.243 |\n| P6 | 1.0083 | 0.8973 to 1.1193 | 0.846 |\n| P7 | 0.9612 | 0.8129 to 1.1095 | 0.508 |\n| P8 | 0.9754 | 0.8915 to 1.0594 | 0.463 |\n| P9 | 1.0426 | 0.8602 to 1.2249 | 0.552 |\n| P10 | 0.9902 | 0.8293 to 1.1510 | 0.873 |\n| P11 | 0.9466 | 0.7424 to 1.1507 | 0.508 |\n| P14 | 1.0821 | 0.8864 to 1.2777 | 0.309 |\n\n- Every 95% CI includes 1.\n- The lowest p value is 0.243 (P5). P5 has a mean above 1.\n- Five plasmid means are below 1: P4 (0.9657), P7 (0.9612), P8 (0.9754), P10 (0.9902) and P11 (0.9466).\n- For these five plasmids, the data are compatible with a lower rate. Their CIs reach values below 1. The lowest lower limits are 0.7424 for P11 and 0.7957 for P4.\n- The mean of the 12 plasmid means is 1.0092. The calculate step gave this value from the 12 relative means in the table.\n\nSteps that gave these numbers: the compare step gave the table, the 95% CIs and the p values. The calculate step gave the mean of the 12 means.\n\n## Uncertain\n\n- The CIs are wide. For several plasmids, the data cannot rule out a substantial reduction in growth rate. A large reduction is compatible with these results.\n- Each plasmid has only 5 blocks. The record does not say whether each block is an independent culture. If blocks are technical replicates, the number of independent replicates is smaller.\n- Twelve tests were run. I did not correct the p values for multiple testing. No p value is near 0.05, so a correction would not change which tests are significant.\n- The record gives no reason for excluding blocks 2 and 12. Excluding these blocks removes both Host and plasmid wells from the comparison.\n- I did not test lag time or maximum growth rate.\n\n## Files\n\n- Fit plot: fit_growth_curves-3/plot.png\n- Comparison table: compare_growth-3/groups.csv\n- Comparison plot: compare_growth-3/plot.png\n\n## Waiting for you\n\n- Confirm the reason for excluding blocks 2 and 12. The fit and the comparison used this exclusion.\n- Decide whether a larger number of replicate cultures per plasmid is needed before you make a claim about any plasmid's effect on growth.\n\nSettings used, from the decision record: Background correction: min · Medium-only wells for the blank: none · Last time point of the fit: 0 · Unit of the time column: h · Wells that you exclude: W10, W11, W12, W13, W14, W15, W16, W17, W18, W80, W81, W82, W83, W84 · Points in each window of the lag time method: 5 · Reference strain or condition: Host · Divide by the reference mean or by the reference well of the same block: same block.",
